<h2>The 12 Best Roofing Marketing Blogs for Lead Generation and Growth</h2>

<p>These are the blogs that publish original, tested marketing strategies specifically for roofing contractors. They are not generic marketing blogs that occasionally mention roofing. They are written by people who understand storm season cash flow, insurance supplement workflows, and the difference between a retail lead and a hail damage lead.</p>

<h3>1. Roofing Webmasters Blog — Nolen Walker</h3>

<p>Nolen Walker founded Roofing Webmasters in 2013 after his own frustrating experiences with marketing agencies while running a home services business. His blog is the most technically deep roofing marketing resource on the internet. Walker does not publish fluff. He publishes 2,000-word guides on Google Maps ranking factors, E-E-A-T signals for roofing websites, and why most roofer blog posts generate zero traffic.</p>

<p>His core thesis is simple: most roofing SEO advice from generalist gurus is wrong for contractors. Walker argues that service pages with recent job photos outperform generic blog posts for local rankings. His proprietary DataPins software automates this process by pulling actual project data into website content. If you want to understand why your website is not ranking in the Map Pack, start here.</p>

<h3>2. Hook Agency Blog — Tim Brown</h3>

<p>Tim Brown built Hook Agency from a two-person shop into a 55-plus person agency specializing in home service contractors. His roofing marketing blog covers SEO, paid ads, website design, and lead magnets with a focus on persuasive copywriting. Brown is particularly strong on emotional benefit-driven messaging, a technique most roofing contractors ignore in favor of feature lists.</p>

<p>Hook Agency's case studies show real numbers: 200 percent year-over-year increases in first-page rankings, 92.98 percent increases in qualified organic leads, and $143 cost-per-conversion with Google Ads. Brown also publishes profit margin analysis for roofing companies, helping contractors understand what they can realistically afford to spend on marketing.</p>

<h3>3. Roofer Marketing Heroes Blog — Chris Hunter</h3>

<p>Chris Hunter has built over 1,055 roofing websites and generated more than 703,000 appointments for contractor clients. His blog, Roofer Marketing Heroes, publishes practical guides on SEO, Google Maps optimization, PPC, video marketing, and AI tools for roofers. Hunter's "Ultimate Guide to Digital Marketing for Roofers" is one of the most downloaded resources in the industry.</p>

<p>What sets Hunter apart is his willingness to share exact systems. He has published the complete framework that grew one roofing company from $350,000 to $3 million in two years. That level of transparency is rare in contractor marketing.</p>

<h3>4. Local Roofing SEO Agency Blog</h3>

<p>This blog focuses exclusively on local search domination for roofing contractors. Their 2026 digital marketing guide covers Google Business Profile optimization, citation building, review generation, and local content strategies. The blog is particularly valuable for contractors in competitive markets like Dallas, Houston, and Phoenix who need to outrank established competitors.</p>

<h3>5. BuildRight Digital Blog</h3>

<p>BuildRight Digital publishes actionable roofing marketing ideas with a strong emphasis on SEO and content marketing. Their 2026 guide covers 17 specific marketing tactics, from storm damage content strategies to direct mail campaigns that still work in older neighborhoods. The blog is written for contractors who want to execute marketing themselves rather than outsource everything.</p>

<h3>6. Red Brick Web Blog</h3>

<p>Red Brick Web specializes in marketing strategies for roofing companies, with a focus on storm damage marketing and review generation. Their blog breaks down how to create cost-comparison content that attracts high-intent homeowners in the research phase. This is critical because homeowners who search "how much does a roof replacement cost" are typically 30 to 60 days from making a purchase decision.</p>

<h3>7. AMRA and Elma Blog</h3>

<p>AMRA and Elma publish data-driven roofing marketing statistics and industry trend reports. Their 2026 statistics compilation is one of the most cited resources in roofing marketing circles. If you need current data on cost-per-click trends, homeowner behavior shifts, or marketing budget benchmarks, this is your source.</p>

<h3>8. Roofing Business Partner Blog — Adam Sand</h3>

<p>Adam Sand runs Roofing Business Partner and is a certified SumoQuote implementation partner. His blog and podcast content focus on building marketing and sales funnels that contractors actually own, rather than depending on lead brokers. Sand's five key tips for roofing growth include nailing service-market fit, tracking the right KPIs, delivering a five-minute customer experience, and avoiding the "CRM doom loop" that paralyzes so many contractors.</p>

<h3>9. Roofing Success Blog — Jim Ahlin</h3>

<p>Jim Ahlin co-founded Roofer Marketers and co-authored "Internet Marketing For Roofing Contractors: How to Triple Your Sales." While his primary platform is the Roofing Success Podcast, the accompanying blog publishes detailed show notes, marketing frameworks, and guest insights from industry leaders. Recent topics include speed-to-lead optimization and 2025 year-end lessons that every contractor should apply in 2026.</p>

<h3>10. Minyona Blog — Michael Mignogna</h3>

<p>Michael Mignogna runs Minyona, a Baltimore-based digital marketing agency for roofing contractors. His Scrappy Wins podcast and blog focus on marketing that actually works for home service providers. Mignogna also runs the Minyona Contractor Systems community on Skool, where paying members get exclusive training on converting leads into deals, including selling roofs through Facebook.</p>

<h3>11. ServiceTitan Roofing Blog</h3>

<p>ServiceTitan is the dominant software platform for home service contractors, and their roofing blog reflects that scale. They publish comprehensive guides on roofing industry trends, business growth strategies, and marketing efficiency. Their 2026 market report surveyed over 1,000 roofing companies and found that 75 percent expect revenue growth, yet only 16 percent follow up with homeowners same-day for unsold estimates. That gap is a massive marketing opportunity.</p>

<h3>12. AccuLynx Blog</h3>

<p>AccuLynx is the leading CRM for roofing contractors, and their blog publishes 92 roofing marketing ideas alongside operational advice. While AccuLynx is primarily a sales and project management tool, their marketing content covers lead intelligence, automation workflows, and photo-based marketing strategies that help contractors turn project documentation into sales assets.</p>

