<h2>The 8 Essential Roofing Industry Publications for Market Intelligence</h2>

<p>Marketing without industry context is like roofing without knowing the pitch. These publications keep you informed about material costs, labor shortages, insurance industry shifts, and regulatory changes that directly impact your marketing messaging.</p>

<h3>1. Roofing Contractor Magazine</h3>

<p>Roofing Contractor Magazine is the premier resource for roofing professionals and the official publication of the International Roofing Expo. Published by BNP Media, it covers business management, new products, safety regulations, and insurance developments. The magazine produces the annual Top 100 and Top 150 Roofing Contractors rankings, which offer valuable competitive intelligence.</p>

<p>For marketing purposes, Roofing Contractor Magazine is essential because it reveals where the industry is heading. When the magazine covers new building codes or insurance carrier policy changes, smart contractors adjust their marketing messaging immediately. For example, when insurance carriers began shortening acceptable roof ages to 15 to 20 years, contractors who updated their website content and ad copy to address this trend captured a wave of anxious homeowners.</p>

<h3>2. Professional Roofing Magazine</h3>

<p>Professional Roofing is the official magazine of the National Roofing Contractors Association (NRCA). It covers technical research, government regulations, workforce development, and business management. The magazine is free with an NRCA membership and offers both print and digital subscriptions.</p>

<p>Recent coverage has included AI applications in roofing, mental health initiatives for workers, and bipartisan housing legislation that affects contractor demand. Marketing-savvy contractors use this publication to identify emerging trends before competitors, then create content around those topics to capture early search traffic.</p>

<h3>3. NRCA Blog and Resources</h3>

<p>The National Roofing Contractors Association publishes technical manuals, training programs, and advocacy updates. Their 2025 Roofing Manual: Steep-slope Roof Systems is the industry standard. For marketers, the NRCA's workforce and regulatory updates provide content angles that resonate with both commercial and residential audiences.</p>

<h3>4. RoofersCoffeeShop</h3>

<p>RoofersCoffeeShop is an award-winning online community that has served the roofing industry for over 20 years. Founded by Heidi J. Ellsworth and Vickie Sharples, it combines industry news, podcasts, forums, and classified ads. The site covers technology adoption, sustainability innovations, and association events.</p>

<p>What makes RoofersCoffeeShop valuable for marketing is its community-driven content. The forums reveal real contractor pain points, which become content ideas. The podcasts feature interviews with successful contractors who share what actually worked in their marketing. Their sister site, MetalCoffeeShop, extends this coverage to metal construction.</p>

<h3>5. GAF Blog</h3>

<p>GAF is the largest roofing manufacturer in North America, and their blog publishes product innovation updates, installation best practices, and contractor program information. While manufacturer blogs are often promotional, GAF's content provides valuable material for contractor websites. When GAF releases a new shingle line or warranty update, contractors who publish timely content about these changes capture search traffic from homeowners researching products.</p>

<h3>6. Owens Corning Roofing Blog</h3>

<p>Owens Corning emphasizes sustainability and material science innovation in their content. Their blog covers SureNail technology, TruDefinition color platforms, and Platinum Preferred Contractor program updates. Contractors certified with Owens Corning can leverage this content to build trust with homeowners who prioritize brand-name materials and comprehensive warranties.</p>

<h3>7. CertainTeed Roofing Blog</h3>

<p>CertainTeed positions itself as the premium alternative to GAF, and their blog reflects that focus. Content covers luxury shingle lines, design inspiration, and Select ShingleMaster certification requirements. For contractors targeting high-end residential markets, CertainTeed's blog provides the technical depth needed to justify premium pricing in marketing materials.</p>

<h3>8. Atlas Roofing Asphalt Life Blog</h3>

<p>Atlas Roofing launched Asphalt Life in 2017 as a resource for both contractors and homeowners. The blog covers business strategies, sales training, and casual lifestyle content. Atlas also provides extensive marketing resources for contractors in their Atlas Pro program, including logo usage guidelines, promotional materials, and digital tools like the Shingle Visualizer.</p>

