<h2>The 6 Roofing Podcasts That Will Change How You Think About Marketing</h2>

<p>Podcasts are the ultimate multitasking learning tool for contractors who spend hours driving between job sites. These six shows deliver marketing insights you can implement the same day.</p>

<h3>1. The Roof Strategist Podcast — Adam Bensman</h3>

<p>Adam Bensman's podcast is the most followed free roofing sales training network in the industry, with millions of views across platforms. Episodes run 10 to 22 minutes and drop every Monday and Thursday. Bensman covers retail roofing sales, storm damage sales, door-to-door canvassing, and objection handling.</p>

<p>While primarily a sales podcast, the marketing implications are massive. Bensman teaches contractors how to craft pitches that convert, which directly informs ad copy, landing page headlines, and email subject lines. He is also the official sales training partner for Owens Corning and author of "The Roofing Sales Survival Guide."</p>

<h3>2. Roofing Success Podcast — Jim Ahlin</h3>

<p>Jim Ahlin interviews roofing industry leaders about digital marketing, lead generation, and business scaling. The podcast covers SEO, paid advertising, website optimization, and operational systems. Recent episodes have explored speed-to-lead strategies and year-end lessons from 2025 that contractors must apply in 2026.</p>

<h3>3. Roofer Growth Hacks — Chris Hunter</h3>

<p>Chris Hunter's podcast focuses on digital marketing trends, growth strategies, and expert interviews. With 23 years of online marketing experience, Hunter brings a depth of knowledge that goes beyond surface-level tips. His monthly "state of the industry" episodes help contractors understand which marketing channels are working right now versus which ones are fading.</p>

<h3>4. Roofing SEO Podcast — Nolen Walker</h3>

<p>Nolen Walker's podcast delivers short-form SEO education in 11 to 16 minute episodes. He covers Google Maps ranking, website content strategy, review generation, and branding. Walker's approach is refreshingly direct: he tells roofers exactly what to do, what to avoid, and why most SEO advice from generalist gurus is wrong for contractors.</p>

<h3>5. Scrappy Wins — Michael Mignogna</h3>

<p>Michael Mignogna's podcast is for contractors who want marketing that actually works. Episodes average 23 minutes and feature both educational content and long-form interviews with actual clients. Mignogna focuses on practical strategies for Facebook marketing, lead conversion, and building marketing systems that do not require a PhD in digital advertising.</p>

<h3>6. Hook Better Leads — Tim Brown</h3>

<p>Tim Brown's podcast covers marketing, sales, leadership, and mindset for roofers and contractors. Episodes explore lead generation, conversion optimization, and the psychology behind why homeowners choose one contractor over another. Brown's background in persuasive copywriting makes this podcast particularly valuable for contractors who want to improve their messaging.</p>

